  Repaint this grey block mockup as a finished video game asset line-up: building types of one medieval town standing side by side along a cobbled street. 16-bit SNES pixel art, isometric 2:1 projection, warm earthy palette (browns, tans, terracotta, forest green, stone grey, gold, deep red, sky blue), single dark outline, medium shading, light from the top left, medieval central European, 14th century. Crisp pixels, no blur, no text, no UI. Keep EXACTLY the camera, the position, footprint and height of every building, the streets, the water and the little people: the people are 1.7 m tall adults and set the scale; do not shrink or enlarge any building. From left to right: a one-storey half-timbered cottage, a two-storey half-timbered house, a three-storey patrician house with slate roof, a stone blacksmith forge with a brick chimney and glowing hearth, a small stone chapel with a slate spire, a crenellated town wall segment, a square stone wall tower, and a gothic cathedral with two spired towers and a high nave. Plain grass around them, people walking on the street in front.

